WEBVTT

00:34:59.521 --> 00:35:00.826
than we would otherwise.

00:35:00.850 --> 00:35:03.403
And it meant we were going
to be, like, fully present

00:35:03.427 --> 00:35:04.790
and make eye contact,

00:35:04.814 --> 00:35:08.416
in a way that you might not
in a casual encounter.

00:35:08.440 --> 00:35:10.638
AG: There's something
built into this exercise

00:35:10.662 --> 00:35:13.092
that's sometimes hard
to recreate in everyday life,

00:35:13.116 --> 00:35:16.376
which is, the mutuality
is designed into it.

00:35:16.400 --> 00:35:18.488
It's almost like starting
on a second date,

00:35:18.512 --> 00:35:21.591
where you show up and you know
the person is opted in,

00:35:21.615 --> 00:35:24.442
and they're excited to interact with you.

00:35:24.466 --> 00:35:26.646
And I wondered how you
go about creating that

00:35:26.670 --> 00:35:28.287
outside the exercise.

00:35:29.570 --> 00:35:33.571
JD: Yeah, we have to
prime ourselves, partly,